id: pm-vcs-release-caller-rollout
title: Adopt the released reusable Daily Release caller
description: "Fleet rollout for unbraind/pm-ops#272 after the successful pm-jira cross-repository OIDC pilot. Replace copied release orchestration with the released SHA caller, matching validator, explicit empty changelog hooks and package-owned caller contracts. No merge, dispatch or publication."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: "area:release","gh:unbraind/pm-ops#272"
created_at: "2026-11-14T22:26:50.942Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-16T09:09:04.690Z"
assignee: pi-claude
claim_principal: pi-claude
author: codex-ops272-1114
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-14T22:27:00.144Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Orient and start the authorized fleet rollout. Verified released v2026.11.14 at 7687a35d7522482bd8361d60dbc2589e9afbc81c. Preserve this package approval, schedule, preparation and publication hooks through canonical inputs. The merged Jira pilot proves cross-repository npm identity acceptance; this package must still pass its own first-run preflight. Run caller contracts, installed attestation, strict YAML, actionlint and regenerated changelog checks. Shared-runner hold gates every push. No review-thread action, merge, dispatch or publication."
  "2026-11-14T22:40:31.059Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Rolled the Jira pilot contract into this package: released workflow pin 7687a35d7522482bd8361d60dbc2589e9afbc81c (v2026.11.14), exact pm-ops 2026.11.14 validator, explicit include-empty changelog generation/check/notes hooks, and declared yaml for caller tests. Preserved package-owned approval, schedule and preparation inputs. Focused gates passed 70/70, zero failures/skips; linked caller test passed 6/6 in a scratch pm project to avoid tracker run artifacts. Reverting only release.yml to the old copy in a disposable fixture failed 5 of 6 contracts. Actionlint passed 1/1, strict workflow/Dependabot YAML parsing 2/2, installed publish-attestation passed 1/1. Regenerate changelog and check after this final tracker write. Full npm/Bun certification remains with CI; no full local pass is claimed. Cross-repository npm OIDC evidence is Jira run 43639146392, recorded on pm-ops#272; first package activation must still pass its preflight. This package has no npm trusted publisher: releases remain red at the OIDC step until the owner configures the publisher for this repository and release.yml. Every push waits on the shared-runner hold. No merge, dispatch, publication or review-thread action. Leave this item open and release only this author claim."
  "2026-11-15T02:49:11.044Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Round 2 CI follow-up: canonical tag lookup can return unverified-offline. The old inline-publisher success-message assertion then fails despite a valid caller. Update the package attestation test to assert structured recognition, require an explicit deferral without an attestation claim offline, and preserve all refusal checks. Prove it with forced offline execution in a disposable Git fixture; keep coverage source inventory and thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-11-15T03:10:29.365Z",codex-ops272-1114,"Round 2 attestation follow-up: targeted tests passed 14/14, including the retained caller and package behavior contracts. Forced offline verification explicitly reports unverified-offline and defers attestation; it never claims verified provenance. In a disposable Git fixture, the fixed assertion passes, reverting only to the old assertion fails, and restoring the fix passes. Unattested-publish refusal checks remain intact. Typecheck and lint passed; coverage source inventory and thresholds remain unchanged. Linked tests passed in a copied scratch tracker. Regenerate and check the changelog after this final write. Exact pushed-head npm/Bun coverage and release certification remain CI gates. No merge, release dispatch, publication or review-thread action."
  "2026-11-16T09:08:55.866Z",pi-claude,"Stalled-PR recovery round 3. Root causes of the failing checks: (1) both test jobs failed test-environment's entrypoint audit because the new release-workflow contract test did not isolate before importing the SDK; fixed by importing the session isolation helper as its first statement, matching every other test entrypoint. (2) Node 22 additionally reported a one-descriptor leak in the object-lifetime soak; that test is untouched by this PR and passes locally on repeated runs, so it is treated as a pre-existing runner flake and left for CI to re-verify on the new head. (3) Greptile thread (stale self-host archive) and CodeRabbit thread (release commit carries the preparation stamp outside the bundle source) both addressed: excluded the release candidate stamp from the self-host source set and regenerated the committed bundle so tip-tree equality holds. Coverage retained: unattested-publish refusal checks and caller contracts unchanged; targeted suites 55/55 and the entrypoint audit 6/6 passed locally, plus typecheck and lint."
